      <Value><![CDATA[{
  "contentData": [
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "a34c3bf8-3b46-4f88-9bb0-09b0ed11c963",
      "key": "7c73eced-b113-4e50-bb32-696c31662bca",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "text",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": null,
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EThe art of being strategically lazy\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        },
        {
          "alias": "header",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Caching"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "387fbbea-8c41-4019-ac76-c3e6e590f6e1",
      "key": "ef8309fa-94d6-48f0-817b-8899b8dd98ec",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "richText",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": null,
            "markup": "\u003Cp class=\u0022MsoNormal\u0022\u003EI mentioned in my \u003Cem\u003E\u201C--Headless \u2013 Not Hovedl\u00F8st--\u201D\u003C/em\u003E post that I wanted to follow up with a series of shorter posts.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp class=\u0022MsoNormal\u0022\u003EIt\u2019s been \u003Cstrong\u003Emonths\u003C/strong\u003E.\u003Cbr\u003ESo let\u2019s get to it, starting with caching.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "1495d116-fbc6-4c94-905d-65c841fe85d0",
      "key": "a496b810-76fc-4807-a305-1f8703af1a2e",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "cropPreference",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": [
            "Ratio"
          ]
        },
        {
          "alias": "altText",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "A lone box"
        },
        {
          "alias": "image",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": [
            {
              "key": "97c3d272-6c9f-4013-a686-b19166be8a91",
              "mediaKey": "3be5b3fe-b3fd-472e-94bd-9ef59a737683",
              "mediaTypeAlias": "Image",
              "crops": [],
              "focalPoint": null
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "387fbbea-8c41-4019-ac76-c3e6e590f6e1",
      "key": "24f54b82-b74b-4000-8b1c-0df985497d4b",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "richText",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": null,
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EIf you\u2019re reading this, there\u2019s a good chance I don\u2019t need to convince you that we should \u201C--cache anything cacheable--\u201D. Still, to make sure no one gets left behind, let\u2019s boil the motivation down to its absolute core.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp class=\u0022MsoNormal\u0022\u003EWe cache for two reasons:\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cul style=\u0022margin-top: 0cm;\u0022\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003EPerformance\u003C/strong\u003E\u003C/p\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003ECost\u003C/strong\u003E\u003C/p\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\u003C/ul\u003E\u003Cp class=\u0022MsoNormal\u0022\u003EThat\u2019s it.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp class=\u0022MsoNormal\u0022\u003EBoth of those contain a \u003Cstrong\u003Enear-infinite\u003C/strong\u003E number of sub-reasons, but they all collapse into those two words.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp class=\u0022MsoNormal\u0022\u003EWe want --performance-- because it improves the visitor experience, and because --Google, Amazon, and a long list of very smart people-- have told us it matters.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp class=\u0022MsoNormal\u0022\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003EAmazon\u003C/strong\u003E famously found that every additional 100 ms of page load time reduced sales by roughly 1%.\u003Cbr\u003EGoogle observed that adding \u003Cstrong\u003E500 ms\u003C/strong\u003E to the result page reduced traffic by almost --20%--.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "1495d116-fbc6-4c94-905d-65c841fe85d0",
      "key": "20ef94c2-6f21-4bcb-bf73-0a87bb4aa7c5",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "bottomText",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Weeeeeee"
        },
        {
          "alias": "altText",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Guy going fast on a bike"
        },
        {
          "alias": "cropPreference",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": [
            "Slim"
          ]
        },
        {
          "alias": "image",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": [
            {
              "key": "a006cdd3-f0bd-4ae8-9138-1287f5d4dea5",
              "mediaKey": "24eb25a6-a1fc-4900-ada7-52a62eba1e72",
              "mediaTypeAlias": "Image",
              "crops": [],
              "focalPoint": {
                "left": 0.49232328817620497,
                "top": 0.5396612873360206
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "387fbbea-8c41-4019-ac76-c3e6e590f6e1",
      "key": "5a3e1140-bebb-40e8-9f93-6218de6a2a05",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "richText",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": null,
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EBut also, let\u2019s be honest, --going fast is fun--.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003ECost is a different beast. Being cheap isn\u2019t inherently fun, but happy clients are. And very few things are cheaper than \u003Cstrong\u003Enot executing code at all\u003C/strong\u003E.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EServing content from \u003Cstrong\u003ECloudflare\u003C/strong\u003E or --Azure Front-- Door is dramatically cheaper than load-balancing ten VMs or App Services across multiple regions.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "1495d116-fbc6-4c94-905d-65c841fe85d0",
      "key": "888589fb-a497-449e-8903-f9242a167e47",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "altText",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": ""
        },
        {
          "alias": "cropPreference",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": [
            "Ratio"
          ]
        },
        {
          "alias": "image",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": [
            {
              "key": "e20da37b-f5d9-4360-8878-a598f324de9a",
              "mediaKey": "c25bafd1-b647-4a64-96f0-0907b3097172",
              "mediaTypeAlias": "Image",
              "crops": [],
              "focalPoint": {
                "left": 0.5009222661396574,
                "top": 0.5615394476334269
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "9ede4277-930d-4106-b18c-b3380269d981",
      "key": "0f5f6d11-0f4c-43f7-8433-64542b4daf0d",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "headerTitle",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "**Easy Caching**"
        },
        {
          "alias": "headerLevel",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": [
            "H2"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "387fbbea-8c41-4019-ac76-c3e6e590f6e1",
      "key": "9377abd9-c2e4-428c-b756-592050d236c3",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "richText",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": null,
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EUsing Cloudflare or Front Door is what I\u2019d call easy caching.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EYou can almost just --turn it on--.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EOf course, it comes with sacrifices, like everything else, and in a CMS context one important detail is often forgotten. Caching the output is great, but it\u2019s only useful if it changes when content changes.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EEditors hit --publish--.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EContent gets --updated--.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EMedia is --replaced--.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EAnd yet, many solutions respond to this by invalidating everything.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EWhy?\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EBecause tracking what actually \u003Cstrong\u003Echanged \u003C/strong\u003Eis difficult.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "1495d116-fbc6-4c94-905d-65c841fe85d0",
      "key": "5b07333f-0801-4977-b172-866c5ada62b5",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "altText",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Winding road"
        },
        {
          "alias": "cropPreference",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": [
            "Slim"
          ]
        },
        {
          "alias": "image",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": [
            {
              "key": "5cf46ebf-f18a-44b5-a9a8-c1dce3d0b33c",
              "mediaKey": "e3f8c9cf-a67a-4fce-8652-cb70bfa97424",
              "mediaTypeAlias": "Image",
              "crops": [],
              "focalPoint": null
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "387fbbea-8c41-4019-ac76-c3e6e590f6e1",
      "key": "4a8cd41d-e143-4056-986c-85c99f9ed54f",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "richText",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": null,
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003E--Cache invalidation-- isn\u2019t hard because the tools are bad. It\u2019s hard because content relationships are complex. A single page might reference blocks, media, compositions, and related content that lives somewhere else entirely.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EThat\u2019s why I built \u003Ca target=\u0022\u0022 data-router-slot=\u0022disabled\u0022 href=\u0022https://marketplace.umbraco.com/package/kraftvaerk.umbraco.headless.cachekeys\u0022 title=\u0022marketplace.umbraco.com\u0022 type=\u0022external\u0022\u003EHeadless Cache Keys\u003C/a\u003E\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EIt\u2019s a small \u003Cstrong\u003EUmbraco package\u003C/strong\u003E that enriches Content Delivery API responses with a set of cache keys representing all content and media dependencies for a given response.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EThose keys can then be used to selectively --purge-- Cloudflare or Front Door, invalidating only what actually changed.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EI run this on \u003Ca target=\u0022\u0022 data-router-slot=\u0022disabled\u0022 href=\u0022http://Kjeldsen.dev\u0022 type=\u0022external\u0022\u003EKjeldsen.dev\u003C/a\u003E, partly to dogfood it, but also to make the behavior visible. If you inspect the HTML of the page, just before \u0026lt;/body\u0026gt; you\u2019ll find:\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cul style=\u0022margin-top: 0cm;\u0022\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EA timestamp for when the page was cached\u003C/p\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EAll cache keys associated with that response\u003C/p\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\u003C/ul\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "f618abe7-aaac-4ad7-927c-4d39b15c975d",
      "key": "9b6c4d48-b61d-4ee6-8117-e4ff42250d81",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "code",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "\u0060\u0060\u0060html\r\n\u003C!-- Cache Keys (12) | ISO: 2026-02-03T12:08:13.461Z \r\n| UTC: Tue, 03 Feb 2026 12:08:13 GMT | CacheEnabled: true \r\n| MaxAge: 86400 | Segment: default \r\n| DerivedKeyPart: /blog/headless-not-hovedloest/-default\r\n--\u003E\r\n\u0060\u0060\u0060\r\n"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "387fbbea-8c41-4019-ac76-c3e6e590f6e1",
      "key": "e45f7833-4e6a-4c17-b426-180551f46f49",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "richText",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": null,
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EAt a high level, the flow looks like this:\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cul style=\u0022margin-top: 0cm;\u0022\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003ERegister \u003C/strong\u003Ea NotificationHandler in Umbraco\u003C/p\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003EReact \u003C/strong\u003Eto publish events\u003C/p\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003EExtract \u003C/strong\u003Eaffected URLs via cache keys\u003C/p\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003ESend \u003C/strong\u003Ea targeted purge request to your CDN\u003C/p\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\u003C/ul\u003E\u003Cp\u003EYou can see a full example of this using Azure Front Door here:\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003Ca target=\u0022_blank\u0022 data-router-slot=\u0022disabled\u0022 href=\u0022https://github.com/kasparboelkjeldsen/kjeldsen.dev/blob/main/kjeldsen.backend/code/notifications/ContentSaved/ContentSavedCacheKeyLogger.cs\u0022 title=\u0022github.com\u0022 type=\u0022external\u0022\u003EToo long to include in blogpost :)\u003C/a\u003E\u003Cbr\u003E\u003Cbr\u003EThere is, however, a practical limitation.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp class=\u0022MsoNormal\u0022\u003EAzure Front Door purges can take up to ten minutes to complete.\u003Cbr\u003ECloudflare is faster, but still not instant.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp class=\u0022MsoNormal\u0022\u003EThat\u2019s not a technical problem. It\u2019s an --editor expectation problem--, and one you need to align on early.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "1495d116-fbc6-4c94-905d-65c841fe85d0",
      "key": "23533f73-d001-426c-8e33-f1934870c4c5",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "cropPreference",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": [
            "Slim"
          ]
        },
        {
          "alias": "altText",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Bunch of dials"
        },
        {
          "alias": "image",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": [
            {
              "key": "62b9e9ab-ed36-4508-8cf9-11b242632f11",
              "mediaKey": "8020d9f3-6329-468a-9aec-d211c1e5a373",
              "mediaTypeAlias": "Image",
              "crops": [],
              "focalPoint": null
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "9ede4277-930d-4106-b18c-b3380269d981",
      "key": "64d76802-d63a-4465-905d-517391204189",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "headerTitle",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "--Advanced Caching--"
        },
        {
          "alias": "headerLevel",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": [
            "H2"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "387fbbea-8c41-4019-ac76-c3e6e590f6e1",
      "key": "21f56c2f-da34-4678-aadc-dd27b2db6f52",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "richText",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": null,
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003ENow let\u2019s say you want invalidation \u003Cstrong\u003ENOW\u003C/strong\u003E.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp class=\u0022MsoNormal\u0022\u003EMaybe ten minutes is --unacceptable--.\u003Cbr\u003EMaybe you don\u2019t want to cache your HTML responses at the \u003Cstrong\u003ECDN\u003C/strong\u003E layer. You should still keep Cloudflare or Azure Front Door in front of your site, since they also give you TLS termination, WAF, rate limiting, and traffic control, not just caching.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp class=\u0022MsoNormal\u0022\u003EOr maybe --(and this is the interesting one)--, your content varies by visitor \u003Cstrong\u003Esegment\u003C/strong\u003E.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp class=\u0022MsoNormal\u0022\u003EAll good reasons.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp class=\u0022MsoNormal\u0022\u003EThe third case (personalization) is what pushed me to move my caching layer closer to the application. I run Umbraco Engage on \u003Ca target=\u0022\u0022 data-router-slot=\u0022disabled\u0022 href=\u0022http://Kjeldsen.dev\u0022 type=\u0022external\u0022\u003EKjeldsen.dev\u003C/a\u003E, and once you have visitor segments influencing content, a CDN caching by URL alone can\u0027t tell the difference between a segmented visitor and a default visitor hitting the same path. You either serve the wrong content, or you stop caching entirely. Neither is acceptable.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp class=\u0022MsoNormal\u0022\u003EI run \u003Cstrong\u003EUmbraco Engage\u003C/strong\u003E there, mostly to experiment and understand how it behaves internally. But it introduces a challenge that CDN caching alone doesn\u2019t solve well. Personalized responses.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp class=\u0022MsoNormal\u0022\u003EYes, this is technically solvable with --Cloudflare Enterprise--.\u003Cbr\u003ENo, I don\u2019t think \u201CContact Sales\u201D pricing belongs in this blog post.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp class=\u0022MsoNormal\u0022\u003ESo what does \u201Ccloser to the application\u201D mean?\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp class=\u0022MsoNormal\u0022\u003EIt means this:\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cul style=\u0022margin-top: 0cm;\u0022\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003EMedia, JS, CSS, and static assets\u003C/strong\u003E are still served and cached by the CDN\u003C/p\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EHTML responses are rendered server-side\u003C/p\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EThe cache lives inside the application\u003C/p\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\u003C/ul\u003E\u003Cp class=\u0022MsoNormal\u0022\u003EIf a response is cached, no meaningful code runs.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp class=\u0022MsoNormal\u0022\u003EBecause I\u2019m using \u003Cstrong\u003ENuxt\u003C/strong\u003E with a headless CMS, I rely on \u003Cstrong\u003ENuxt Multi Cache\u003C/strong\u003E, which provides route-level caching among other things. The specific package isn\u2019t important. Any SSR framework can do this. Behavior is what\u2019s important.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp class=\u0022MsoNormal\u0022\u003EInstead of purging a --CDN--, I invalidate the application cache directly when Umbraco publishes content.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp class=\u0022MsoNormal\u0022\u003EThat invalidation is effectively \u003Cstrong\u003Einstant\u003C/strong\u003E.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "9ede4277-930d-4106-b18c-b3380269d981",
      "key": "045088c2-850b-495c-992e-365a4e5934d6",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "headerLevel",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": [
            "H3"
          ]
        },
        {
          "alias": "headerTitle",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "**Caching and Personalization**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "387fbbea-8c41-4019-ac76-c3e6e590f6e1",
      "key": "7d4fd985-1b25-44ab-870e-98849a0d7dee",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "richText",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": null,
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EThis is where things get tricky.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp class=\u0022MsoNormal\u0022\u003ELet\u2019s say you have a page that\u2019s personalized.\u003Cbr\u003ETo keep it simple, imagine a blog post that shows a picture of a \u003Cstrong\u003Edog\u003C/strong\u003E or a --cat-- depending on whether the visitor is on desktop or mobile.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "387fbbea-8c41-4019-ac76-c3e6e590f6e1",
      "key": "bc296c76-9fd8-4ecf-ae62-24d5ae476a74",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "richText",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": null,
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EIt\u2019s tempting to conclude that this page shouldn\u2019t be --cached--.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp class=\u0022MsoNormal\u0022\u003EAnd sometimes, that\u2019s \u003Cstrong\u003Etrue\u003C/strong\u003E.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp class=\u0022MsoNormal\u0022\u003EIf content is --hyper-personalized--, tied to a visitor ID, name, or individual behavior, caching can explode into thousands of variations and quickly become \u003Cstrong\u003Ecounterproductive\u003C/strong\u003E.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp class=\u0022MsoNormal\u0022\u003EBut if content varies by segment, and you have a small, bounded number of segments, caching is still very much on the table.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp class=\u0022MsoNormal\u0022\u003EThe key is constructing the right cache key.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp class=\u0022MsoNormal\u0022\u003ECDNs typically cache by URL:\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp class=\u0022MsoNormal\u0022\u003E--a.b.c/my-page--\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp class=\u0022MsoNormal\u0022\u003EApplication caches don\u2019t have that limitation.\u003Cbr\u003EThey can include anything available at request time.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp class=\u0022MsoNormal\u0022\u003EOn \u003Ca target=\u0022\u0022 data-router-slot=\u0022disabled\u0022 href=\u0022http://Kjeldsen.dev\u0022 type=\u0022external\u0022\u003EKjeldsen.dev\u003C/a\u003E, the cache key for a server-rendered page is constructed from:\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cul style=\u0022margin-top: 0cm;\u0022\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EThe page URL\u003C/p\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EThe value of the \u003Cstrong\u003EengageSegment\u003C/strong\u003E cookie (--that I set--)\u003C/p\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\u003C/ul\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "f618abe7-aaac-4ad7-927c-4d39b15c975d",
      "key": "c62bc810-52d6-4dac-a795-4fa6678548e2",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "code",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "\u0060\u0060\u0060ts\r\n\r\nimport { defineMultiCacheOptions } from \u0027nuxt-multi-cache/server-options\u0027\r\nimport { getRequestURL, getHeader } from \u0027h3\u0027\r\n\r\n/**\r\n * Global multi-cache server options\r\n * - Adds segment aware route cache key: {path}::seg:{segmentAlias}\r\n * - segmentAlias comes from engageSegment cookie (short alias) or defaults to \u0027default\u0027\r\n */\r\nexport default defineMultiCacheOptions(() =\u003E {\r\n  return {\r\n    route: {\r\n      buildCacheKey(event) {\r\n        const url = getRequestURL(event)\r\n        const path = url.pathname || \u0027/\u0027\r\n\r\n        // Skip cookie logic if in preview mode\r\n        if (url.searchParams.has(\u0027engagePreviewAbTestVariantId\u0027)) {\r\n          return \u0060${path}::seg:default\u0060\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        // Access cookie header manually (avoid allocating cookie parser for perf)\r\n        let segment = \u0027default\u0027\r\n        try {\r\n          const cookieHeader = getHeader(event, \u0027cookie\u0027) || \u0027\u0027\r\n          if (cookieHeader) {\r\n            const match = cookieHeader.match(/(?:^|; )engageSegment=([^;]\u002B)/)\r\n            match \u0026\u0026 match[1] \u0026\u0026 (segment = decodeURIComponent(match[1]))\r\n          }\r\n        } catch (e) {\r\n          // Fallback to default if cookie access fails (e.g. cross-origin iframe restrictions)\r\n          segment = \u0027default\u0027\r\n        }\r\n        // Normalize segment alias to safe subset\r\n        if (!/^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{1,64}$/.test(segment)) segment = \u0027default\u0027\r\n        return \u0060${path}::seg:${segment}\u0060\r\n      },\r\n    },\r\n  }\r\n})\r\n\r\n\u0060\u0060\u0060"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "387fbbea-8c41-4019-ac76-c3e6e590f6e1",
      "key": "1e9a25bd-9707-455f-a52e-f23f531fade0",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "richText",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": null,
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EThat means a single page might generate two cache entries:\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp class=\u0022MsoNormal\u0022\u003E--a.b.c/my-page::seg:desktop-user--\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp class=\u0022MsoNormal\u0022\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003Ea.b.c/my-page::seg:default\u003C/strong\u003E\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp class=\u0022MsoNormal\u0022\u003EReading a cookie during request handling is no more expensive than reading the URL itself. It\u2019s already part of the request and adds no meaningful overhead.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp class=\u0022MsoNormal\u0022\u003EA first-time visitor will naturally fall back to the default segment. If your setup requires immediate segmentation, for example based on IP, geography, or time of day, you can perform a one-off personalization pass on the initial request using middleware. --(I use the middleware approach)--\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp class=\u0022MsoNormal\u0022\u003EThis still allows segmented content to be cached safely, without sacrificing correctness or \u003Cstrong\u003Eperformance\u003C/strong\u003E.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "9ede4277-930d-4106-b18c-b3380269d981",
      "key": "b49c6cdf-8cb0-4cfb-8880-973eec2ff976",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "headerTitle",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "**Wrapping Up**"
        },
        {
          "alias": "headerLevel",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": [
            "H2"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "387fbbea-8c41-4019-ac76-c3e6e590f6e1",
      "key": "be26af84-5b38-426c-8817-5eb4b1d79ad9",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "richText",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": null,
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003ECaching isn\u2019t a --switch you flip--.\u003Cbr\u003EIt\u2019s a set of deliberate trade-offs.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp class=\u0022MsoNormal\u0022\u003ECDN caching is cheap, fast, and incredibly effective. But the moment you care about when content changes, who it changes for, or how quickly those changes should be visible, you --may-- need more control.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp class=\u0022MsoNormal\u0022\u003EThe rule I tend to follow is this:\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp class=\u0022MsoNormal\u0022\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003ECache as close to the user as possible and as much as possible,\u003Cbr\u003E--but invalidate as close to the truth as necessary and as little as possible.--\u003C/strong\u003E\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp class=\u0022MsoNormal\u0022\u003ESometimes that truth lives in a CDN purge.\u003Cbr\u003ESometimes it lives inside your application.\u003Cbr\u003ESometimes it depends on a cookie, a segment, or a publishing event that happened milliseconds ago.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp class=\u0022MsoNormal\u0022\u003EWhat you should avoid is defaulting to --\u201Cclear everything\u201D-- because it feels simpler. That\u2019s not simplicity. It\u2019s giving up control, observability, and performance.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp class=\u0022MsoNormal\u0022\u003EOr --clear everything--. Maybe it\u0027s right for your use case. All I really want is to explore what\u0027s possible and reliable and rant about it, and if you made it this far. I hope some of it was interesting.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp class=\u0022MsoNormal\u0022\u003EIn the next post, I\u2019ll stay in the same headless space but shift focus slightly, securing the Content Delivery API.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp class=\u0022MsoNormal\u0022\u003EBecause once you start caching aggressively and serving content fast, you also need to be very clear about who is allowed to fetch what, and why. Umbraco currently has --one-- Api-Key to the kingdom. Lets\u0027 change that.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003Cspan style=\u0022font-size: 12pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif;\u0022\u003ECaching may be the art of being --strategically lazy--.\u003Cbr\u003ESecurity is the art of being \u003C/span\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003E\u003Cspan style=\u0022font-size: 12pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif;\u0022\u003Edeliberately strict\u003C/span\u003E\u003C/strong\u003E\u003Cspan style=\u0022font-size: 12pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif;\u0022\u003E.\u003C/span\u003E\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "2fbb5f26-eb3b-443e-80ac-5699dcbab4ea",
      "key": "535435aa-4447-47e4-b827-64178b63802f",
      "values": []
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "a34c3bf8-3b46-4f88-9bb0-09b0ed11c963",
      "key": "40edf8eb-53d5-4dd4-848f-0090972bdba8",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "text",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": null,
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EHere there was supposed to be a whole cute thing with me showing either a cat or dog dependant on your viewing device and a segmentation rule in Umbraco Engage. I had even enabled block level segmentation in Umbraco and worked around it not being a complete feature yet - but someone killed my Engage License by hitting my frontpage about 6000 times a day for the last month.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003Cimg src=\u0022?rmode=max\u0026width=347\u0026height=363\u0022 width=\u0022347\u0022 height=\u0022363\u0022 data-udi=\u0022umb://media/308510dd5ecc4a9da3cdc8b57432f4ec\u0022\u003E\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E:(\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003Cbr\u003ESo for now I will show both images and let you use your imagination (and block certain kinds of requests in my WAF - and more importantly no-longer forward them to Umbraco Engage)\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        },
        {
          "alias": "header",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Note as of the 27th of March"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
